"""Sparse lexical/orthographic approximation; not a general semantic classifier.

Selected penal-law and insect morphemes give positive responses. Vietnamese
x+em/x+ong and long-aa sequences in Indic/Arabic scripts give negative ones.
Small additional rules cover 星, some Thai/Japanese/Korean spellings, repeated
middle dots, and a document-opening NUL. Unlisted positions return 0.001.
A 16-byte tail recognizes split characters and resets at document boundaries.
This intentionally leaves most fine-grained contextual variation unmodeled.
