Use word boundaries, case, fragment length and consonant clusters, with a
stronger response to the string abbreviation str. Word-internal endings
are weaker. Single-letter transliterations of S also get weaker responses.
Coarse document-start baselines and repeated interpunct runs cover two
additional observed effects. These rules omit token-specific exceptions.
"""
